@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@
+# Metamorphic Intelligence Execution Ledger
+
+## Objective
+
+Activate HSE's existing staged evidence/claim/inference intelligence model on real persisted scan state without changing current scan promotion semantics. Produce a bounded, auditable read-only projection first; use real execution evidence from that projection before considering any semantic cutover.
+
+## Authoritative baseline
+
+- Repository: `EmmmmDeee/Huntsman-Search-Engine-HSE-Termux-Android-Aarch64-Rust-`
+- Branch: `main`
+- Baseline commit: `ff8e850977c9fb4cc36817eb1830bc12d17e9a32`
+- Baseline tree: `7dd7cbb11984afc1ad0903a47a648e6bce0bbe24`
+- Baseline package: `huntsman-search-engine 1.41.0`, Rust 2024, MSRV 1.98.
+- `hse-core::Evidence` already preserves source, summary, attributes, observation time, verification, inference status, and scan provenance.
+- Existing HSE corroboration logic already distinguishes raw observation magnitude from distinct corroborating sources and excludes deterministic enrichment/recall/engine-only promotion paths.
+- `src/core/intelligence.rs` already implements immutable-style evidence records, source lineage, claims, inferences, hypotheses, provider coverage, falsification conditions, and independent-lineage claim promotion.
+- Verified production gap: `src/core/intelligence.rs` explicitly states that nothing in the production scan pipeline constructs an `IntelligenceLedger`; current scan promotion still uses `Entity::confidence`.
+
+## Acceptance priorities
+
+CORRECTNESS → SAFETY → DATA INTEGRITY → FUNCTIONAL COMPLETENESS → INTEGRATION → RELIABILITY → RECOVERABILITY → OBSERVABILITY → PERFORMANCE → MAINTAINABILITY → SIMPLICITY.
+
+## Competing solutions evaluated
+
+### A — Immediate promotion-semantic cutover
+
+Use `IntelligenceLedger::ClaimState` directly to replace current entity/correlation promotion.
+
+Rejected for this increment. It changes production semantics, storage/API expectations, and could regress mature scan behavior before the staged model has been exercised on real persisted scans.
+
+### B — Read-only staged-ledger projection
+
+Project existing persisted entities and correlations into the staged ledger without mutating the database or current promotion behavior.
+
+Selected. It is reversible, independently verifiable, exposes the strongest existing epistemic machinery to real data, and provides evidence required to evaluate a later cutover.
+
+## Implemented increment
+
+### `src/core/intelligence_projection.rs`
+
+- Deterministic persisted scan → `IntelligenceLedger` projection.
+- Raw entity evidence remains authoritative and is never mutated or overwritten.
+- Every projected evidence item retains a pointer to the authoritative `(entity_uid, evidence_index)` source slot.
+- Direct observations become `EvidenceNature::Observed`.
+- Inferred, enrichment-only, and engine-corroboration records remain visible as `Derived` but cannot support an observation claim.
+- Existing source-lineage metadata is consumed when present (`source_id`, `record_id`, `publisher_id`, `origin_id`, `origin`, `corpus`, `dataset`, `source_record_id`).
+- No retrieved-content digest is manufactured from an extracted summary. A content digest is preserved only when the source supplied one (`content_digest`, `source_digest`, or `sha256`).
+- In the absence of explicit origin metadata, source/module identity provides a conservative reporting-family fallback.
+- Each persisted entity becomes an evidence-backed `observed_entity` claim.
+- Correlations do **not** inherit endpoint evidence. Each correlation becomes a separate relationship claim plus an `Inference` whose premises are the endpoint observation claims.
+- Because an inference is not a witness, a relationship claim remains `Candidate` until future direct relationship evidence supports it.
+- Correlations whose persisted endpoints are incomplete are counted as unprojected gaps and are not partially inferred.
+- Alternative explanations, strengthening/weakening conditions, and falsification conditions are attached to projected claims/inferences.
+- SHA-256-derived evidence, claim, and inference IDs are deterministic for identical inputs.
+
+### `src/api/scan_handlers/intelligence.rs`
+
+- Adds read-only `GET /api/v1/scans/{id}/intelligence` projection.
+- Reuses the existing entity candidate quarantine before projection.
+- Removes correlations touching hidden candidate endpoints so relationship descriptions cannot bypass the privacy gate.
+- Defaults to 1,000 projected visible entities and hard-caps the endpoint at 5,000 for Termux/Android memory safety.
+- Reports visible/projected/omitted entity and correlation counts and an explicit `truncated` flag; bounded output cannot masquerade as exhaustive output.
+
+### `src/bin/intelligence-audit/main.rs`
+
+- Adds a read-only database audit executable for real persisted scans.
+- Accepts an explicit scan ID and optional database path.
+- Defaults to 5,000 entities and hard-caps at 100,000.
+- Filters correlations to projected endpoints and reports whether output was truncated.
+- Emits JSON suitable for deterministic comparison and regression fixtures.
+
+### Existing-file integration
+
+- `src/core/mod.rs`: register `intelligence_projection`.
+- `src/api/scan_handlers/mod.rs`: register/re-export `scan_intelligence`.
+- `src/api/routes/mod.rs`: register `/api/v1/scans/{id}/intelligence` and document it in the route table.
+- `Cargo.toml`: explicitly register the `intelligence-audit` developer binary.
+
+## Falsification / regression locks included
+
+1. Same-source observations remain one independent witness and cannot promote an entity claim.
+2. Independent source lineages can promote an entity observation claim to `Supported`.
+3. Derived/enrichment evidence is preserved but never attached as observation support.
+4. Different publishers sharing one explicit origin remain one reporting family.
+5. Correlations become inferences and cannot self-promote their relationship claim from endpoint evidence.
+6. Missing correlation endpoints produce a recorded projection gap, not a partial relationship inference.
+7. A retrieved-content digest is not invented when the source did not supply one.
+8. Identical input produces identical evidence/claim/inference identifiers.
+
+## Resource and failure semantics
+
+- Projection is read-only: no SQLite migration and no persistent mutation.
+- API projection is bounded; truncation is explicit.
+- Candidate gating executes before projection.
+- Projection invariant violations return a 500 with explicit failure detail rather than a false empty result.
+- Missing scan IDs fail loudly.
+- Existing scan behavior remains the fallback/authoritative production path because this increment does not alter promotion.
+
+## Validation state
+
+### Demonstrated
+
+- Authoritative `main` head rechecked immediately before packaging and remains `ff8e850977c9fb4cc36817eb1830bc12d17e9a32`.
+- Existing staged-ledger contracts and exact `Inference` shape were verified against repository source.
+- Existing `IntelligenceLedger` is serializable and its insertion/promotion semantics were verified from source.
+- Static delimiter and artifact-integrity checks completed locally.
+- GitHub write permission was tested through three independent mechanisms: branch refs, Git object creation, and Contents API. All return `403 Resource not accessible by integration`, establishing a connector permission blocker rather than an inferred blocker.
+
+### Not demonstrated in this environment
+
+- `cargo fmt`
+- Rust compilation
+- clippy
+- unit/integration tests
+- aarch64 cross-build
+- real persisted-scan execution
+- HTTP endpoint runtime exercise
+- GitHub integration/CI
+
+Reason: the execution container has no Rust toolchain and no external DNS route; the connected GitHub integration is read-capable but rejects every tested write path with 403.
+
+No unexecuted item above is represented as passing.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Baseline: `ff8e850977c9fb4cc36817eb1830bc12d17e9a32`.
+
+The increment has no storage migration. Before integration, rollback is simply discarding the patch branch/worktree. After a verified fast-forward merge, rollback is a normal code revert of the integration commit; persisted scan data is unchanged.
+
+## Exact restart sequence
+
+1. Restore a GitHub/checkout write path and confirm `main` still equals or descends unchanged from the baseline above.
+2. Apply the supplied integration bundle in a clean checkout.
+3. Run `cargo fmt --all -- --check`.
+4. Run focused tests for `intelligence_projection`.
+5. Run `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`.
+6. Run the repository's full locked test/gate commands without weakening existing gates.
+7. Build the production `hse` binary and the `intelligence-audit` binary.
+8. Run `intelligence-audit` against a real persisted scan and verify deterministic output, independent-source counts, Candidate relationship claims, and explicit truncation/gaps.
+9. Run `hse serve`, call `/api/v1/scans/<REAL_SCAN_ID>/intelligence`, verify candidate quarantine and bounded-scope metadata.
+10. Run the repository's existing Android/aarch64 build/gate.
+11. Only if all preceding checks pass, fast-forward the validated integration to `main` and push.
+12. Re-fetch remote `main`, verify its SHA is the validated commit, and rerun the operator-facing smoke path.
+13. Only after this real evidence exists should promotion-semantic cutover be reconsidered.
